1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,100
Right before the 4th of July, a crypto bill that was supposed to sail through the Senate stalled.

2
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:08,820
Most people shrugged, just another bill stuck in Washington.

3
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:13,700
But the thing jamming it up is a question that sounds way too small a matter.

4
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:15,700
Can a stablecoin pay you interest?

5
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:21,140
And that tiny sounding question is hiding one of the biggest money moves of the decade.

6
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:26,940
Because while everyone argues about interest, two bills are quietly doing something much bigger,

7
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:32,120
keeping the US dollar on top for another 50 years, and they're doing it with crypto.

8
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:37,800
The Genius Act already signed into law, and the Clarity Act, the one stuck in the center right now.

9
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:41,380
Together they turned stablecoins into a Trojan horse for the dollar.

10
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:42,800
Let me show you the whole play.

11
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:48,300
After World War II, the world's gold had drained into one country, the United States.

12
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:50,600
So everyone else did the practical thing.

13
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:54,900
They pegged their money to the dollar because the dollar was redeemable for gold.

14
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:57,800
The dollar became the world's reserve currency.

15
00:00:57,960 --> 00:00:59,860
Then America started abusing it.

16
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:03,220
It printed far more dollars than it had gold to back them.

17
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:07,460
By the late 60s, the world caught on and came to collect.

18
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:08,820
There wasn't enough gold.

19
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:12,920
So in 1971, Nixon slammed the gold window shut.

20
00:01:13,380 --> 00:01:14,900
The gold standard was dead.

21
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:18,340
Losing the reserve currency would have ended American power.

22
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:21,420
So they invented a new leash, the petrodollar.

23
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:23,560
Oil would only be priced in dollars.

24
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:28,160
Every nation on earth that wanted oil first had to get US dollars.

25
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:31,880
And those dollars flowed back into US Treasuries.

26
00:01:32,260 --> 00:01:32,860
That's the trick.

27
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:34,480
Every single time.

28
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:39,820
Force the world to need dollars and then soak those dollars back into American debt.

29
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:41,220
No gold required.

30
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:43,240
Just leverage over everyone.

31
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:47,520
And it held for 50 years until it started slipping again.

32
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:50,880
So fast forward to today where the dollar is slipping again.

33
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:51,920
Same story.

34
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:55,120
They're printing far more than the economy can absorb.

35
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:56,580
They needed a new leash.

36
00:01:57,180 --> 00:01:58,560
And they just legislated one.

37
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:00,740
Here's the part almost nobody connects.

38
00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:04,400
A dollar stablecoin isn't just magic internet money.

39
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:09,000
Behind every coin, the issue where parks actual dollars in US Treasuries.

40
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:14,820
And in July of 2025, this month last year, that stopped being optional.

41
00:02:14,940 --> 00:02:16,540
The Genius Act became law.

42
00:02:16,540 --> 00:02:23,820
It forces every dollar stablecoin to hold 100% reserves in cash and short term US Treasuries.

43
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:25,640
Read what this actually means.

44
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:31,300
Every dollar stablecoin on the planet is now a forced buyer of American government debt.

45
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:32,000
By law.

46
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:35,380
The petrodollar funneled the world's money into Treasuries.

47
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:39,760
Stablecoins funding the world's everyday money into Treasuries.

48
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:40,600
Same trick.

49
00:02:41,220 --> 00:02:41,720
New rails.

50
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:43,900
This is Bretton Woods 3.0.

51
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:46,880
And this time, the dollar doesn't need gold.

52
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:48,480
The dollar doesn't need oil.

53
00:02:48,780 --> 00:02:50,980
It just needs your phone.

54
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:56,760
And speaking of your phone, the best thing you could do with it right now is to scroll down

55
00:02:56,760 --> 00:03:00,960
on that description, tap on that link to join the community.

56
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:02,520
The best community ever.

57
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:03,340
My community.

58
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:09,740
We make tons of software where 50 X's and 100 X's are just commonplace these days.

59
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:13,280
And if you like this content, make sure you click that like button

60
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:14,760
and that subscribe button.

61
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:18,320
And click that bell icon too so you never miss content like this.

62
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:22,540
Because in a second, I'm going to show you the part that almost nobody gets right.

63
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:24,860
There's a real interest ban on the books.

64
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:28,100
And you're probably earning interest on your stables right now.

65
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:30,180
Here's a loophole that explains why.

66
00:03:30,420 --> 00:03:34,320
Now, every government on earth wants a central bank digital currency.

67
00:03:34,540 --> 00:03:35,100
One ledger.

68
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:36,380
Total visibility.

69
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:39,020
Control over every transaction you make.

70
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:39,860
There's one problem.

71
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:42,020
Their own citizens don't want it.

72
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:46,880
A government coin that watches every single dollar you spend is a surveillance tool

73
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:48,180
and people know it.

74
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:51,120
So most of those projects are frozen in pilot mode.

75
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:51,920
Going nowhere.

76
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:54,100
So Washington did something smarter.

77
00:03:54,300 --> 00:03:55,980
It didn't build a government coin.

78
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:59,300
It let private companies build a dollar coin.

79
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:01,360
Then wrote the laws to control them.

80
00:04:01,460 --> 00:04:03,380
It's not run by the central bank.

81
00:04:03,980 --> 00:04:06,800
It's regulated by Congress and enforced by the treasury.

82
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:08,200
Same control.

83
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:09,640
None of the stigma.

84
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:11,620
That is the Trojan horse.

85
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:18,360
A quasi private central bank digital currency that the people install themselves because

86
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:20,560
it just looks like a better bank account.

87
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:22,000
Nobody writes over it.

88
00:04:22,340 --> 00:04:23,160
Nobody cares.

89
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:25,600
Nobody writes over an app that pays them.

90
00:04:25,900 --> 00:04:27,140
And that's exactly the point.

91
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:29,380
So here's the part that everyone trips up.

92
00:04:29,580 --> 00:04:31,040
And honestly, it tripped me up too.

93
00:04:31,220 --> 00:04:33,980
There's a real interest ban, but it's not in the clarity act.

94
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:36,820
And it does not do what people think it does.

95
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:40,140
The ban is in the genius act and that one's already law.

96
00:04:40,140 --> 00:04:43,780
And it says the issuer of a stable coin, a company like Circle,

97
00:04:44,340 --> 00:04:46,680
cannot pay you yield just for holding their coin.

98
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:51,680
The funny thing is that you're probably still earning yield on your stable coins right now.

99
00:04:51,820 --> 00:04:54,200
So that begs the question, like what gives?

100
00:04:54,520 --> 00:04:56,060
The ban stops at the issuer.

101
00:04:56,340 --> 00:04:57,860
It never touches the exchanges.

102
00:04:58,900 --> 00:04:59,940
Circle can't pay you.

103
00:05:00,140 --> 00:05:04,640
But Coinbase can hand you about three and a half percent and call it a loyalty reward

104
00:05:04,640 --> 00:05:06,800
because Coinbase isn't the issuer.

105
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:08,320
Same money, same interest.

106
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:12,200
It just takes one extra hop so it doesn't count as the issue we're paying you.

107
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:14,440
The law has a Coinbase shaped hole in it.

108
00:05:14,460 --> 00:05:18,320
And that hole is worth over a billion dollars a year to Coinbase alone.

109
00:05:18,640 --> 00:05:20,800
So now the banks want that hole closed.

110
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:22,900
Regulators are proposing closing it.

111
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:25,740
And the clarity act, the one stuck in a center right now,

112
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:27,680
is where the fight is playing out.

113
00:05:27,740 --> 00:05:29,900
That's the real reason that clarity matters.

114
00:05:30,220 --> 00:05:32,160
Not because it bans interest,

115
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:35,940
but because it decides whether or not that loophole lives or dies.

116
00:05:35,940 --> 00:05:38,360
Whether you keep earning interest on your stable coins

117
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:42,680
and hellhard America gets to sell the dollar to the rest of the world.

118
00:05:42,820 --> 00:05:47,480
Which is why this boring sounding bill matters more than the price of any coin this month.

119
00:05:47,660 --> 00:05:49,200
And the timing is everything.

120
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:53,880
Right now the US government is drowning in debt and it needs the world to keep buying.

121
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:57,000
Long term treasury yields are near multi-decade highs.

122
00:05:57,580 --> 00:05:58,900
Real demand is thin.

123
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:01,440
Every time America needed to sell more debt

124
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:03,900
it manufactured new users of the dollar.

125
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:05,340
Gold gave it Bretton Woods.

126
00:06:05,340 --> 00:06:07,060
Oil gave it the petrodollar.

127
00:06:07,280 --> 00:06:08,960
Now crypto gives us stable coins.

128
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:13,040
Estimates put the new treasury demand in the trillions over the coming years.

129
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:16,340
A fresh captive lender for the bankrupt government.

130
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:18,560
Built out of the world's everyday money.

131
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:21,480
So at the exact moment that the world is asking

132
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:24,100
how long is the dollar gonna last from here?

133
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:29,060
Washington's answer is to put the dollar into everybody's hand on the entire planet.

134
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:31,080
Not by force, by choice.

135
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:35,920
And behind the scenes your purchasing power gets funneled straight into the debt.

136
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:40,620
Papering over their spending and pushing the price of everything you actually need higher.

137
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:43,240
If you think that they won't use that to their advantage

138
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:45,440
then you haven't been paying attention.

139
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:49,380
I used to think that the dollar has about 20 or 30 years left.

140
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:52,720
But this right here guarantees it for at least another 50.

141
00:06:52,940 --> 00:06:56,500
Which is exactly why smart money isn't holding a dollar right now.

142
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:58,920
It's holding things it can't print.

